they want to spend more.

00:21:13.472 --> 00:21:15.607
The Democrats always, when
they have the White House,

00:21:15.607 --> 00:21:18.076
oh, Republicans want to
shut down the government.

00:21:18.076 --> 00:21:19.778 align:start size:97% position:3%
I want to say no, no, we won't
shut down the government,

00:21:19.778 --> 00:21:23.081 align:start size:97% position:3%
but we'll spend at some
current level minus something,

00:21:24.216 --> 00:21:25.817
and then you can
have a real debate.

00:21:25.817 --> 00:21:27.552
Because if we don't, we'll
get into the crazy stuff.

00:21:27.552 --> 00:21:29.721
So that's what I want
on the debt ceiling,

00:21:29.721 --> 00:21:31.523
that structural change.

00:21:31.523 --> 00:21:32.891
We'll see if we can get that.

00:21:32.891 --> 00:21:34.760
- Do you ever think
maybe a shutdown

00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:36.228
wouldn't be the worst thing?

00:21:36.228 --> 00:21:37.763
I mean, they always frame
it as this is gonna be

00:21:37.763 --> 00:21:39.264
the worst thing ever, but
I'm kind of coming around

00:21:39.264 --> 00:21:41.433 align:start size:97% position:3%
to the idea of, okay, let then
